 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532926,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You want to repair a window on the second floor of your home. If you place the ladder at a <span data-math=\"{30^ \\circ }\">{30^ \\circ }</span> angle to the ground, the ladder just about reaches the window. How far from the wall should you place the ladder? How far up will the ladder reach? Make a sketch as an aid.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/e8d0b8766c31cd77.png\" alt=\"An illustration shows a 34-foot ladder placed against a building at an angle of 30 degrees. The vertical distance from the ladder to the ground is marked b. The horizontal distance from the base of the building to the base of the ladder is a.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The set of ratios in a 30°-60°-90° triangle are <span data-math=\"1:\\sqrt 3 :2\"></span>, or <span data-math=\"x:x\\sqrt 3 :2x\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since you are shown the right angle are told about the 30° angle at the ground, you know the other angle is a 60° angle.</p>\n<p>The ladder is the longest side, so <span data-math=\"2x = {\\text{ }}24\"></span> feet.</p>\n<p>If <span data-math=\"2x = {\\text{ }}24\"></span>, then <span data-math=\"x = {\\text{ }}12\"></span> and <span data-math=\"b = {\\text{ }}12\"></span> feet since it is the shorter leg, opposite the 30° angle</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x\\sqrt 3 = 12\\sqrt 3 \\approx 20.8{\\text{ feet}}\"></span>, the distance from the wall.</p>\n<p>The ladder is 20.8 feet (or <span data-math=\"12\\sqrt 3 \"></span> feet) from the wall and reaches 12 feet up the wall.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The ladder reaches 12 feet up the wall and sits <span data-math=\"12\\sqrt {3\\,}{\\text{ feet}}\">12\\sqrt {3\\,}{\\text{ feet}}</span> from the wall."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
